#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064096 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/id #uuid "4d4edfc8-e178-58b4-b827-e4310ead130e" :question/math-academy-id "e-485" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}-1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1} = 4 -\\dfrac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{0}^{1}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[4-0]-5[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =4-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064097 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/id #uuid "74761123-d539-5d78-8dcd-4ea1db04bed0" :question/math-academy-id "e-486" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division. \n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{ 2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3} .\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+3x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064098 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "cf016fa7-c3a2-5f9b-84a6-7b005d0d7286" :question/math-academy-id "e-487" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}\\dfrac12$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $\\dfrac12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-\\dfrac12$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} & =1-\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3043908-006c-5588-93e1-5b803fb93b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-13\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488793} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b71903-4e15-5c97-a27a-a82277649d99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+25\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488796} {:answer/id #uuid "d10b0a2a-281b-50cf-9df5-c0629cd9fd98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6+17\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488896} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d32315-e259-5a8f-81b5-8559a49cf8cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+23\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488952} {:answer/id #uuid "ea677eb7-1d1d-5c70-90b8-646e9f157560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-21\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6d32315-e259-5a8f-81b5-8559a49cf8cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+23\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488952} :answer-field/id #uuid "06e29f29-fb54-5de8-b11c-95711b29f9f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489020}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "338fe155-640c-56d4-b9a0-1883a5de5f4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-114870" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{6x+5}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ 3 & 6 & 5 \\\\  & ↓ & 18 \\\\  & 6 & 23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{6x+5}{x-3}=6+\\frac{23}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6x+5}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6+\\frac{23}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\text{d}x+23\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6x+23\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b4de8c-fd48-5009-9a54-4cc72bda7222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488580} {:answer/id #uuid "602f7a58-aa0d-5239-aff0-b3b9bed87899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488655} {:answer/id #uuid "86d287c6-5af3-5f71-ac33-1bdfa383d111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488735} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b74ce8-0f84-5e27-b15f-4c5b50bab3b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488833} {:answer/id #uuid "ef14abaa-d1c1-55f6-8694-386044979d64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "602f7a58-aa0d-5239-aff0-b3b9bed87899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488655} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dffcd96-ead6-5e86-bc08-c2510b3e38c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "917d59cb-0d0e-5982-9eaf-dc58471e2414" :question/math-academy-id "q-114884" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}-11x+15}{x-5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 5 & 1 & -11 & 15 \\\\  & ↓ & 5 & -30 \\\\  & 1 & -6 & -15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-11x+15}{x-5}=x-6-\\frac{15}{x-5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}-11x+15}{x-5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(x-6-\\frac{15}{x-5})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x-6{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\text{d}x-15{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{x-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{4}-6x\\,{|}_{0}^{4}-15\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-5|\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({4}^{2}-{0}^{2})-6(4-0)-15(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-5|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0-5|) \\\\  & =8-24-15(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) \\\\  & =15\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9826cc-221a-58f0-a949-003259d10830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247516} {:answer/id #uuid "1935d4e4-d30d-5335-ab50-3b3fa04366e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(1+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247651} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9aeadf-fded-5a2b-861d-58af4c73c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247959} {:answer/id #uuid "54ac800d-c455-530d-b963-3aea2be7c145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248185} {:answer/id #uuid "6b902fe9-3b07-57e2-870c-2a793e643e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b902fe9-3b07-57e2-870c-2a793e643e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248379} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3226bde-c895-54e8-98cf-b5b2df79f6fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "462b058c-0216-5b9a-aa39-6bb6d7bc768e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114896" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $6$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & 2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & 2 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} & =2+\\frac{(\\frac{2}{3})}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{4}{6x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}(2+\\frac{4}{6x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{4}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(0-(-\\frac{1}{12}))+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(0)+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(-\\frac{1}{12})+1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(\\frac{1}{12})+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7df8ea6d-2722-5e70-bbe1-0a201a4aa86d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7df8ea6d-2722-5e70-bbe1-0a201a4aa86d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488723} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f25635d-33d3-5d2f-833b-3ac59e8b2074" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489027} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89da8b57-6aa7-5061-b1f9-ea1ede95ef75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89da8b57-6aa7-5061-b1f9-ea1ede95ef75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488746} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dccc6d6-4e07-52b6-aa1f-ccd35dea7409" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "acd22109-423d-5919-a6a9-ac45c008ca7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-347279" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,16\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-15$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-16$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x-1}{x+3}=5-\\frac{16}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(5-\\frac{16}{x+3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-16{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5x\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =5(2-0)-16(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+3|) \\\\  & =10-16(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =10-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{5}{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57ff2dad-d5e5-593e-86ec-4698166b14ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57ff2dad-d5e5-593e-86ec-4698166b14ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488637} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fe45463-7063-51ad-b0c8-17b9c4472315" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d2e4b25-5dfe-5374-a345-308700b857ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d2e4b25-5dfe-5374-a345-308700b857ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488752} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc8786d3-722f-5eda-bf54-b92884842c57" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8c284bd6-ffb5-522e-9bbf-08c92df09daa" :question/math-academy-id "q-347424" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7x-2}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{13}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7x-2}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7x-2}{3(x+1/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7x-2}{(x+1/3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{3}$ | $7$ | $-2$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{7}{3}$ |\n|  | $7$ | $-\\frac{13}{3}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x-2}{(x+1/3)} & =7-\\frac{(13/3)}{(x+1/3)} \\\\  & =7-\\frac{13}{3x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7x-2}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(7-\\frac{13}{3x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[7{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x-13{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[7x-\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[7(1-0)-\\frac{13}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[7-\\frac{13\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}-\\frac{13}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca46dcc7-5754-5e7c-92d1-ba637f7c916a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca46dcc7-5754-5e7c-92d1-ba637f7c916a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488882} :answer-field/id #uuid "42bf671d-7377-5737-abbb-6129f5300442" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c335ec0-d582-57a9-816c-a4ab3bfc31d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c335ec0-d582-57a9-816c-a4ab3bfc31d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488718} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ed473a7-2cf4-592b-b794-efbb9e644086" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "660f8bdc-c1bb-5f91-9301-9db16573b0bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-352210" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{6x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $6$ | $5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-12$ |\n|  | $6$ | $-7$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{6x+5}{x+2}=6-\\frac{7}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{6x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(6-\\frac{7}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}x-7{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6x{|}_{1}^{3}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =6(3-1)-7(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3+2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2|) \\\\  & =12-7(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =12-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{5}{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eaa259b-afa9-5deb-8159-7c3b66adff9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9eaa259b-afa9-5deb-8159-7c3b66adff9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319866} :answer-field/id #uuid "aec87038-1d77-52ab-aafa-5ef7ab429461" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320515} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adb6b3c7-0cf3-5820-a797-a5dce7bcb453" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adb6b3c7-0cf3-5820-a797-a5dce7bcb453" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319919} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7dd8807-4f91-542d-a4c2-b9b261609c6d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "420b9f17-222f-5f30-947e-edc02435b92c" :question/math-academy-id "q-352220" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $9$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-36$ |\n|  | $9$ | $-29$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}=9-\\frac{29}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}(9-\\frac{29}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\text{d}x-29{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9x\\,{|}_{-1}^{2}-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =9(2-(-1))-29(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-1+4|) \\\\  & =27-29(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =27-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{3}) \\\\  & =27-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,2\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "670a9950-a271-5914-906f-7c59c303960d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "670a9950-a271-5914-906f-7c59c303960d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488668} :answer-field/id #uuid "0070775b-9f73-577e-b7c2-e7c44a14f81e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2deec6cb-34cd-58b8-9f65-c2378d9ee6e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2deec6cb-34cd-58b8-9f65-c2378d9ee6e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488568} :answer-field/id #uuid "997889a6-16e3-5caf-b27f-6c611d20e9f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f97a62fc-8484-5bdf-88ea-0edae07612ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-352232" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{15x+4}{x+6}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,86\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-6$ | $15$ | $4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-90$ |\n|  | $15$ | $-86$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{15x+4}{x+6}=15-\\frac{86}{x+6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{15x+4}{x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}(15-\\frac{86}{x+6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\text{d}x-86{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x+6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15x\\,{|}_{1}^{5}-86\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+6|\\,{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =15(5-1)-86(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5+6|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+6|) \\\\  & =60-86(\\operatorname{ln}⁡11-\\operatorname{ln}⁡7) \\\\  & =60-86\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{11}{7}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489231 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "971e21a4-35f1-5a29-ba6e-cbf260b798f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "971e21a4-35f1-5a29-ba6e-cbf260b798f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488775} :answer-field/id #uuid "17c83049-3bba-5626-8130-3871dbe37307" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "198fdf6b-a075-5de2-8b17-668c98530091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "198fdf6b-a075-5de2-8b17-668c98530091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488524} :answer-field/id #uuid "76fddc9d-060b-5c62-80a7-51c466e021a5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e5fb422-3b84-5ae8-83c2-850e3c9cae23" :question/math-academy-id "q-352242" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{2}+6x+5}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $6$ | $5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-3$ | $-9$ |\n|  | $1$ | $3$ | $-4$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+6x+5}{x+3}=x+3-\\frac{4}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{2}+6x+5}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(x+3-\\frac{4}{x+3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}+3x\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{2}-{0}^{2})+3(2-0)-4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+3|) \\\\  & =2+6-4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =8-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{5}{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6613762c-3532-5365-82fc-bc7a05901a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6613762c-3532-5365-82fc-bc7a05901a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488666} :answer-field/id #uuid "39ab24d6-268c-5219-a363-1c64d249620f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489050} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5c32443-63e9-5fe5-8cce-5815205faa9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5c32443-63e9-5fe5-8cce-5815205faa9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488909} :answer-field/id #uuid "728aa6ab-95a5-58ca-8540-251eb130c4b8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f0dd3c6-cec7-5d16-bef1-1348caabc20b" :question/math-academy-id "q-352244" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+4}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $1$ | $7$ | $4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-2$ | $-10$ |\n|  | $1$ | $5$ | $-6$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+4}{x+2}=x+5-\\frac{6}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+4}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(x+5-\\frac{6}{x+2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x+5{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}x-6{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{3}+5x\\,{|}_{1}^{3}-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|\\,{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{2}-{1}^{2})+5(3-1)-6(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3+2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2|) \\\\  & =4+10-6(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =14-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{5}{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "895cc63e-704d-5c75-8834-1c7f86e88688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "895cc63e-704d-5c75-8834-1c7f86e88688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488742} :answer-field/id #uuid "894843a9-487f-53ee-b815-b69de93ad817" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489089} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f35643b-d2e7-5b1c-8d2c-7d45128e6a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f35643b-d2e7-5b1c-8d2c-7d45128e6a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488504} :answer-field/id #uuid "9063cade-1a05-55db-bbf9-39633e2bd887" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "db6f337c-1879-5d7b-9da6-28f2e468ffa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-352439" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-4}{4x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{31}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-4}{4x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-4}{4(x+\\frac{3}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{3}{4}$ | $5$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{15}{4}$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-\\frac{31}{4}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{4})} & =5-\\frac{(\\frac{31}{4})}{(x+\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{31}{4x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-4}{4x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(5-\\frac{31}{4x+3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-31{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4x+3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[5x-\\frac{31}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+3|]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[5(2-0)-\\frac{31}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|11|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[10-\\frac{31}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{11}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{31}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{11}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "386f7d01-d45d-5b63-bdea-f7097afb83a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "386f7d01-d45d-5b63-bdea-f7097afb83a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488586} :answer-field/id #uuid "b02b234b-d0f9-5546-840a-c2b6b1526301" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bea505c0-e76c-5947-baf4-c73fde66f0aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bea505c0-e76c-5947-baf4-c73fde66f0aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488857} :answer-field/id #uuid "d076e19c-2489-505d-afd3-95862ae4df0b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a5f0f6e3-4d12-5d35-95c5-617c3f9ade1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-358832" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-6}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-6}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-6}{2(x+1/2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-6}{(x+1/2)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $5$ | $-6$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-\\frac{17}{2}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-6}{(x+1/2)} & =5-\\frac{(17/2)}{(x+1/2)} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{17}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-6}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(5-\\frac{17}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x-17{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[5x-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5(1-0)-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5-\\frac{17\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489260 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd25629c-b0db-5e45-b3bf-2761785cbc73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd25629c-b0db-5e45-b3bf-2761785cbc73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488929} :answer-field/id #uuid "083f66af-b3f8-5233-ad8f-5e2cf12ce1ac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489023} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8212502b-b36e-58f1-8b4a-6f28d8e4ba45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8212502b-b36e-58f1-8b4a-6f28d8e4ba45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488729} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6bf3e9-c56c-59e7-96b4-ea6184a4aa6b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ae6c8955-529c-5030-96d7-68d6213f0d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-358833" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x-5}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{19}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x-5}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x-5}{3(x+1/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x-5}{(x+1/3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{3}$ | $4$ | $-5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{4}{3}$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-\\frac{19}{3}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-5}{(x+1/3)} & =4-\\frac{(19/3)}{(x+1/3)} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{19}{3x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x-5}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-\\frac{19}{3x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-19{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[4x-\\frac{19}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4(2-0)-\\frac{19}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[8-\\frac{19\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{19}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ee8549-dcde-5e2d-b477-844548bb8889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488472} {:answer/id #uuid "046bbf35-1798-5517-b212-a873fff0f207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488480} {:answer/id #uuid "419e91d5-4cc1-5e66-91a8-098b7c668264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488605} {:answer/id #uuid "7add5fad-a470-5ad9-a2be-c661c44ca519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488715} {:answer/id #uuid "bc50e037-003f-5b13-a4f3-394595a58447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc50e037-003f-5b13-a4f3-394595a58447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488850} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c099a74-f4bd-5e62-a5f8-8aa1f58a48aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f013a040-e69b-50f7-a6cc-a90f687ce812" :question/math-academy-id "q-49356" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\  & 2 & -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-1}{x-1}=2{x}^{2}-x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{2}-x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1}+x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2[\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}]-[\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}]+[1-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42e6b1e1-c481-5131-aa9b-e51fd0e84f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-4x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488608} {:answer/id #uuid "4a697176-e9f1-5136-bc2c-f4d7b21c4c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488616} {:answer/id #uuid "62d7902c-29ca-5bc3-8e15-8a29b24dccf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488659} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9d1eb3-ac76-5c9d-9822-7053bfb20d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488844} {:answer/id #uuid "e00dd37b-1e6f-5de4-8259-64c1940bd61a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-17x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a697176-e9f1-5136-bc2c-f4d7b21c4c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488616} :answer-field/id #uuid "943cb8b2-64c1-553e-80f2-f883b3ab8a15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea9dfa89-06eb-5760-a821-cda00c20e204" :question/math-academy-id "q-49458" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-17x+4}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $4$ | $-17$ | $4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $16$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-17x+4}{x-4}=4x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}-17x+4}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
